{"author":{"id":"1e0a6ff3e01313072cf7b3803c158c22d01a37717237fe198e814e781752b172"},"ops":[{"type":6,"timestamp":1785445000,"nonce":"NAdyftJ/1ntrrxDZCnpv0zNigKM=","target":"9ff9da8dcbc412077fee999c56359b673cd6ef992f46d1684c0d9ba412eb8b6d","message":"Marc Kleine-Budde \u003cmkl@pengutronix.de\u003e writes:\n\nHello Konstantin,\n\nin yesterday's the OpenEmbedded Workshop 2026 after to FOSDEM we talked\nabout OE's \"Upstream-Status\" tag [1].\n\nThe intended use-case of this tag is to track the upstream status of the\npatches placed in OE board support packages. When mainlining these\npatches, currently one has to remove the tag manually or by some\nscript/automatism.\n\nSo the idea was to add a feature to b4 to automatically remove the\n\"Upstream-Status\" tag when sending patches, or in general have a\nconfigurable list of tags to automatically remove.\n\nWhat do you think?\n\nregards,\nMarc\n\n[1] https://docs.yoctoproject.org/current/ref-manual/qa-checks.html#patch-status\n\n(via 20260202-positive-pristine-malamute-23b575-mkl@pengutronix.de on users@kernel.org)","files":null}]}